## Human-Readable Strings

```xiom
pub interface Display {
  fn fmt(self: &Self, f: &mut Formatter) -> Result[(), FmtError];
}
```

### Implementing Display

```xiom
pub type Point = { x: Float64; y: Float64; }

impl Display for Point {
  fn fmt(self: &Point, f: &mut Formatter) -> Result[(), FmtError] {
    return f.write_str("(" + self.x.to_str() + ", " + self.y.to_str() + ")");
  }
}

fn main() {
  let p = Point{ x: 10.5, y: 20.3 };
  io.println(p.to_str());  // (10.5, 20.3)
  io.println("Point: ${p}");  // Point: (10.5, 20.3) — string interpolation
}
```

### Display vs Debug

- **Display**: User-facing, clean, formatted for readability (dates, prices, coordinates)
- **Debug**: Developer-facing, shows internal state, no formatting promises

### Formatting Patterns

```xiom
impl Display for Temperature {
  fn fmt(self: &Temperature, f: &mut Formatter) -> Result[(), FmtError] {
    return f.write_str(self.celsius.to_str() + "°C");
  }
}

impl Display for Money {
  fn fmt(self: &Money, f: &mut Formatter) -> Result[(), FmtError] {
    let dollars = self.cents / 100;
    let remaining = self.cents % 100;
    return f.write_fmt("${dollars}.{remaining:02}");
  }
}
```

